{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444603-2-0-beasts-recognizing-each-other","id":444603,"title":"2.0. Beasts recognizing each other","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-16T11:31:21-07:00","id":444603,"title":"2.0. Beasts recognizing each other","content":"In the new vampire core rules it was mentioned as a sidenote that they feel that werwwolves have some sort of beast inside of them (thus they feel at unease near them). But it was never implied further there. In the new core for werewolf I didn't see any mentioning there at all about their wolfish side in regards to vampires (how they feel) or if they also feel something from vampires or not.<br /> Did I overlook something there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T11:37:19-07:00","id":444630,"title":"","content":"Where does it say that? I think it just says that 'when they notice' werewolves they get a sort of scared reaction. Not that they instantly recognize werewolves or that they have a beast in them. If it does say that it may be referring to the spiritual aspect of their soul, as they are part unearthly predator. Based on the wording (I'm still using Blood and Smoke, so if you're using VtR2e, our books may say different things) it seems like it's how they feel instead of Lunacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-16-2015, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T11:44:48-07:00","id":444638,"title":"","content":"&quot;When Kindred notice <br /> werewolves, they feel physiological responses they <br /> never otherwise experience, such as goose pimples <br /> along their arms, and chills down their backs. They <br /> feel the adrenaline surge in the pit of the stomach <br /> that humans associate with danger and tense <br /> excitement.<br /> Other creatures in the World of Darkness may <br /> exhibit predatory auras with Storyteller discretion.&quot;<br /> <br /> Right from the rulebook (I hope It is ok that I just copy/paste it from the blood &amp; smoke pdf (if not pls moderator feel free to delete/modify).<br /> <br /> page 92 on the vampire core rules (blood &amp; smoke)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T11:49:31-07:00","id":444641,"title":"","content":"Yeah that's what mine says too. It seems to fit with the book's description of Lunacy, which is described as, 'Lunacy is the deep down, ancestral fear of the wolf at the door.'<br /> <br /> Since vampires aren't affected by Lunacy enough to get the conditions, a sense of 'danger and tense excitement' might fill that space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T11:58:17-07:00","id":444649,"title":"","content":"Which is the question if its enough for them to identify the werewolf as another predator although unknown or not. AND what about the other side if werewolves feel that the vampires are also predators or not (its a bit too vague there for me to interpret it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T12:03:57-07:00","id":444654,"title":"","content":"Just based on 'when they notice' and abilities like Sheep's Clothing, I wouldn't think it grants them an immediate werewolf-detection as much as a reaction for when folks werewolf out, like through changing or healing fast or other things that might cause Lunacy. Of course certain disciplines unearth that type of secret as well, though they no longer have Auspex's aura detection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T14:44:13-07:00","id":444922,"title":"","content":"Auspex 2 can still detect if you're a supernatural being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T15:09:18-07:00","id":444962,"title":"","content":"What that text means is actually what you thought, Ryu, based on my own reading of it. It's talking about how vampires 'notice' werewolves just like they recognize their own kind. So, to me, that doesn't mean they must use some power to discern it, it means just that, they 'notice' them (That is, see or otherwise sense them) and then get that sensation. I'm fairly certain it has nothing to do with lunacy; it's them dealing with a foreign, powerful predator. You'll note it mentions predatory aura, which means it works like noticing other vampires' auras; you simply react on sight.<br /> <br /> Now, the penalty caused by Sheep's Clothing might mean an ST will rule you need a Wits + Composure -2 roll or something to actually sense the aura in the first place when in a crowd or amongst others in general, since they're harder to notice that way, but that's up to individual STs.<br /> <br /> That said, Werewolf's core does not cover other auras. The Hunter's Aspect is meant to be their own aura mechanic, but whoever wrote it decided not to actually interweave what it says with the mechanics elsewhere in the book, or other Aura types like the Predatory Aura. Honestly, that whole section feels rushed and incomplete to me.<br /> <br /> My personal ruling would be a werewolf can sense a vampire like they can other werewolves (A roll when close enough to smell), but that's just a personal interpretation.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And yes, Auspex 2 still detects supernaturals, you just need to specifically 'ask' if they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 03-16-2015, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T15:10:33-07:00","id":444964,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Aura Sight is still a thing, functionally. It's just more intuitive and less charty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T17:58:56-07:00","id":445119,"title":"","content":"It seens to be what the text from Vampire 2e is decribing is basically the vampire's reaction to a werewolf's Hunter Aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T03:56:20-07:00","id":445564,"title":"","content":"Felipe is right. I remeber it was said that paragraph was a placeholder for the &quot;Aura mechanics&quot; of werewolves, not an always on instinctual reaction or anything. Of course the specifics were far from being written, hence the somewhat general description of the effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T04:32:14-07:00","id":445581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444603-2-0-beasts-recognizing-each-other?p=445564#post445564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Felipe is right. I remeber it was said that paragraph was a placeholder for the &quot;Aura mechanics&quot; of werewolves, not an always on instinctual reaction or anything. Of course the specifics were far from being written, hence the somewhat general description of the effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not an always on reaction so much as just how they react to the aura same as they react to each others'; a placeholder, yes, but it doesn't change the mechanics from the Kindred side of things. They sense the aura through kindred senses, they don't need to be targeted by Hunter's aspect first.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 03-17-2015, 07:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T04:46:05-07:00","id":445584,"title":"","content":"I think they do have to be targeted by the Aspect to get any reaction, is not a passive reaction to &quot;wow this guy right there is a werewolf&quot; however they managed to find that out (Auspex, maybe? Sheep's Clothing makes it dificult and I don't know if Kindred Senses could work as Wolf Senses to pick a werewolf appart from a crowd through smell or something).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T04:49:36-07:00","id":445586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444603-2-0-beasts-recognizing-each-other?p=445584#post445584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they do have to be targeted by the Aspect to get any reaction, is not a passive reaction to &quot;wow this guy right there is a werewolf&quot; however they managed to find that out (Auspex, maybe? Sheep's Clothing makes it dificult and I don't know if Kindred Senses could work as Wolf Senses to pick a werewolf appart from a crowd through smell or something).</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it's up for debate, but my reading of that section is that while, yes, some of what it describes is meant to be how the hunter's aspect feels, it's still a 'predatory' aura and can be picked up like they would other kindred. Probably not as simple as looking at a large crowd and pointing to the three werewolves that might be in it (because yes, sheep's clothing applies and even kindred wouldn't be quite so easy to pick out), so much as you bump into one on the street, feel the hairs on your neck stand up, and know that it's another Predator, but not a vampire (I doubt you'd inherently know 'werewolf' without prior experience).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T05:09:45-07:00","id":445598,"title":"","content":"If you recall the Predators Aspect doesn't require any willpower to use on mortals. So logically the major tip off would be when the vampire tries to use it and finds they need to force it through. <br /> <br /> That aside I'd probably tie it to the werewolf's emotional state. If they're just passing it doesn't trigger, but if they raise their hackles for any reason that's when the vampire starts to hear the growling in the back of their head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T06:03:09-07:00","id":445689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...]you bump into one on the street, feel the hairs on your neck stand up, and know that it's another Predator, but not a vampire (I doubt you'd inherently know 'werewolf' without prior experience).</div> </div> </div> </div>That does sound like more interesting way to aproach it, yes. I like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}